      "name": "stalled-agent-triage",
      "title": "Stalled-agent triage and bidirectional relay re-entry",
      "description": "Triage incoming work from stalled agents AND govern returning-agent re-entry after another session advanced the repository. Enforces Bidirectional Relay Continuity: write-ahead epic checkpointing at dispatch time paired with the five-step non-destructive takeover and re-entry reconciliation (remote commit and beans delta, epic Live Relay Snapshot, four-way open/draft PR classification, non-destructive worktree/overlay/donor-cache inspection with `claude/salvage-*` rescue instead of `git reset --hard`, and lease-table plus Merge Steward queue resumption). Use when a session or swarm has stalled, timed out, hit a quota cap, or lost its container, when the owner says \"pick up what X was doing\", or whenever an agent returns on its next turn after another agent advanced `main`, PRs, or `beans`.",
